  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\vec{a}=\\hat{i}-\\hat{k}, \\vec{b}=x \\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+(1-x) \\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{c}=y \\hat{i}+x \\hat{j}+(1+x-y) \\hat{k}$. Then $[\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}]$ depends on",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mAF0A",
      "text": "\nonly $y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XDN1Q",
      "text": "\nonly $\\mathrm{x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DvLdD",
      "text": "\nboth $x$ and $y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Kq3i4",
      "text": "\nneither $x$ nor $y$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\vec{a}=\\hat{i}-\\hat{k}, \\vec{b}=x \\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+(1-x) \\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{c}=y \\hat{i}+x \\hat{j}+(1+x-y) \\hat{k}$\n$[\\vec{a} \\vec{b} \\vec{c}]=\\vec{a} \\cdot(\\vec{b} \\times \\vec{c})$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\vec{b} \\times \\vec{c}=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\\nx & 1 & 1-x \\\\\ny & x & 1+x-y\n\\end{array}\\right|=\\hat{i}\\left(1+x-x-x^2\\right)-\\hat{j}\\left(x+x^2-x y-y+x y\\right)+\\hat{k}\\left(x^2-y\\right) \\\\\n& \\vec{a} .(\\vec{b} \\times \\vec{c})=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nwhich does not depend on $\\mathrm{x}$ and $\\mathrm{y}$",
    "image": null
  },
